Vocab/role/Group/knowledge/Hint: What you know — living, worth revisiting
Vocab/role/Group/procedure/Hint: How you go about it — living, worth revisiting
Vocab/role/Group/reuse/Hint: To copy or duplicate — living, worth revisiting
Vocab/role/Group/register/Hint: Added to, never rewritten
Vocab/role/Group/tracking/Hint: Perishable — purge once it is over

Vocab/role/concept/Hint: Idea explained for its own sake
Vocab/role/ref/Hint: Facts you come back to look up
Vocab/role/source/Hint: An outside work you consulted — book, article, video
Vocab/role/guide/Hint: How-to, step by step
Vocab/role/snippet/Hint: Fragment to copy as is
Vocab/role/template/Hint: Starting point to duplicate
Vocab/role/decision/Hint: Settled choice, and why
Vocab/role/log/Hint: What happened, dated
Vocab/role/hub/Hint: Way in to other tiddlers
Vocab/role/project/Hint: A project itself
Vocab/role/tool/Hint: A tool, or a set of tools, used in projects
Vocab/role/task/Hint: One thing to do
Vocab/role/tasklist/Hint: Tasks tracked together
Vocab/role/routine/Hint: Done again and again, on a rhythm
Vocab/maturity/stub/Hint: Too thin to be of use — needs more substance
Vocab/maturity/rough/Hint: All the substance is there, the writing still needs finishing
Vocab/maturity/stable/Hint: Reviewed, reliable, safe to build on
Vocab/lifecycle/active/Hint: In circulation
Vocab/lifecycle/obsolete/Hint: Superseded — do not rely on it
Vocab/lifecycle/archived/Hint: Kept for the record, unmaintained
Vocab/needs/verify/Hint: Its accuracy is in doubt — check it before relying on it
Vocab/needs/refactor/Hint: Overlaps other tiddlers — merge duplicates or pull out what they share
Vocab/needs/split/Hint: Too long or too mixed — break it into atomic tiddlers
Vocab/status/none/Hint: No status
Vocab/status/considering/Hint: Weighed up, not taken on yet
Vocab/status/todo/Hint: Taken on, not started
Vocab/status/doing/Hint: Started and being worked on
Vocab/status/paused/Hint: Started, then set aside
Vocab/status/done/Hint: Finished
Vocab/status/dropped/Hint: Decided against, will not happen
Vocab/priority/2/Hint: Comes first
Vocab/priority/1/Hint: No particular urgency
Vocab/priority/0/Hint: Can wait
Vocab/epistemology/formal/Hint: “What follows necessarily from these premises?” — pure logical deduction from axioms and definitions, on abstract structures (numbers, sets, logical systems); validated by proof
Vocab/epistemology/natural/Hint: “How does the world really work?” — observation and controlled experiment, on natural phenomena that can be isolated and reproduced; validated by confrontation with the data and refutability
Vocab/epistemology/social/Hint: “Why do humans act this way, alone and together?” — empirical observation and interpretation of the meaning of conduct, on human facts hard to isolate, not reproducible and swayed by the observer; validated by the rigour of the inquiry (statistics, fieldwork, comparison) and the plausibility of the interpretations
Vocab/epistemology/hermeneutic/Hint: “What does this object mean, in its context?” — contextual interpretation of a singular object (text, work, culture, event); validated by the coherence of the reading with the object and its context, and by how much it sheds light on the object. The practice of interpretation, not hermeneutics as its philosophy
Vocab/epistemology/applied/Hint: “How do we make it work?” — theories put to the test of practice, on a concrete problem to solve under constraints; validated by the efficacy of the result. Cuts across the other families
Vocab/epistemology/philosophy/Hint: “What is it, and what justifies it?” — conceptual analysis and rational argument, on general notions and fundamental problems (truth, the good, existence, knowledge); validated by the coherence of the arguments and how they stand up to objections. Cuts across the other families
Vocab/regime/traditional/Hint: Validated by use, transmission and proven efficacy — craft know-how, peasant or indigenous knowledge, tacit knowledge (riding a bike, a carpenter's gesture)
Vocab/regime/religious/Hint: Validated by revelation, the authority of a text or a tradition, faith, inner experience — religions, mysticism, wisdom traditions
Vocab/deviation/pseudoscience/Hint: Imitates the natural sciences; bypasses refutability and confrontation with the data — claims a scientific status without submitting to the method (astrology, homeopathy)
Vocab/deviation/pseudomedicine/Hint: Imitates the applied sciences; bypasses proof of efficacy — false cures, false solutions
Vocab/deviation/conspiracy/Hint: Imitates the human and social sciences and hermeneutics; everything is read as a hidden sign, and the absence of proof becomes a proof
Vocab/deviation/esoteric/Hint: Imitates hermeneutics; bypasses the limits the object sets on its reading (Eco) — hidden codes in texts, reading of signs, a secret knowledge reserved for initiates
Vocab/deviation/sophistry/Hint: Imitates the formal sciences and philosophy; bypasses logical validity and honest argument — fallacious reasoning

